NAME  painter turtle small~
SHORT A small painter turtle is here.~
LONG  This small little painter turtle has red stripes on either side of his tiny head.  He must be a baby turtle, only about two or three inches wide at the thickest part of his shell.~
DESCR
Barely wider than a copper coin, this painter turtle cannot be more than a
season old.  Thin red and yellow stripes run back from its blunt little head,
and the edges of its shell are still soft and pliable.  It watches you with
black bead eyes, in no particular hurry to be anywhere at all.
~
