#OBJDATA
#31000
NAME   silver box elia~
SHORT  a small silver box~
DESCR
A small silver box, half-buried in silt, lies here.~
MAT    silver~
TYPE   container 25 A 0 25 100
EXTRA  0 0
WEAR   A
LEVEL  0
WEIGHT 3
COST   0
COND   100
EDESC box lid elia~
The box is worked from a single piece of pale silver, no larger than two cupped
hands.  The letter 'E' is embellished on the lid in a flowing script, and along
the front edge someone has inscribed the name "Elia".  The metal is untouched by
the years -- no tarnish, no dents -- as though time simply refuses to settle on
it.  When you lift the lid the inside is bare and empty, lined with the faint
smell of pond water.~
End

#31001
NAME   journal elia diary~
SHORT  Elia's journal~
DESCR
A slim journal bound in soft blue cloth rests here.~
MAT    paper~
TYPE   trash 0 0 0 0 0
EXTRA  0 0
WEAR   A
LEVEL  0
WEIGHT 1
COST   0
COND   100
EDESC journal diary elia~
The pages are filled with a bright, looping hand.  Most of it is ordinary --
the price of flour, a neighbour's new goat, how tall the beans have grown -- but
the later entries return again and again to Midian.  "M. swears the old apple
tree runs backward," one reads.  "He found a seam in the air beneath it, he
says, a crack where a rotten tree and a living one share the same roots.  He is
so happy I could cry.  I have never seen him so alive as when he is chasing
something no one else believes in."  The final written page simply says: "He has
started calling it a paradox.  I do not like the word, but I like his smile."~
End

#31002
NAME   journals notes midian papers~
SHORT  a heap of frantic notes~
DESCR
A heap of loose, ink-blotted notes has been swept into a pile here.~
MAT    paper~
TYPE   trash 0 0 0 0 0
EXTRA  0 0
WEAR   A
LEVEL  0
WEIGHT 2
COST   0
COND   100
EDESC notes journals papers midian~
The handwriting has decayed along with the man -- once neat, now a cramped and
shaking scrawl.  Whole pages are crossed out.  What survives is grim.  "There is
no undoing it from inside.  Every attempt only widens the seam."  And later:
"The only cut that does not bleed into the rest is the one that removes the
hand that made it.  If I was never here to begin the work, the work was never
begun.  I must take myself out of time entirely -- and I cannot do it myself
without becoming the very paradox I am trying to close."  A final note, underlined
twice: "The way down is a lie of stone.  Look for the rock that is too even to be
a rock.  Press the triangle."~
End

#31003
NAME   triangular rock switch stone~
SHORT  a triangular rock~
DESCR
One stone in the wall is a little too even, a little too triangular.~
MAT    stone~
