EDESC apple rotten mush~
The apple has caved in on itself, brown and soft and crawling with slow decay.
Yet its shape is unmistakably a match for the ripe fruit beneath the living tree
-- the same curve, the same twist of the stem -- as though a single apple were
somehow rotting and whole at once, in two places at the same time.~
End

