The little locket is black with tarnish and its clasp is bent, plainly stolen and
carried a long, careless way.  Thumbing it open reveals a tiny, faded portrait of
a young woman with a kind, laughing face.  Whoever she was, someone once loved
her enough to carry her over their heart.~
End

