#31001
NAME   A narrow cave entrance~
DESCR
The landslide tore this gap open only recently -- the stone at its edges is
still raw and unweathered, pale where the older rock around it is stained dark.
The passage is barely wide enough for one person, and the daylight behind you
dies quickly against the cold, damp air ahead.  Somewhere deeper you can hear
the slow, patient drip of water.
~
