EDESC chair swing swinging~
This once well-built swinging chair is now almost falling apart with wear from the elements.  On the chair back the initials 'E' and 'M' are carved in scrolled lettering that is beginning to crack.  The supports on one side have fallen, and hte grass seems to be taking over the area the swing once sat on.  The chain that hangs the chair is oddly untouched by the elements like the dock and the chair itself, gleaming on it's own.  The links in the chain seem too small to support two people, and you can see no visible welds in the linkage of the almost delicate chain.~
EDESC dock wooden~
This small wooden dock is built on posts that have been dug into the pond floor at intervals every few feet.  The wood is worn with age, splitting in some areas, but still serviceable enough to walk on without too much featr of falling through.  You can see murkey water below the boards of the dock between the gaps.~
End

#31029
NAME   End of A Small Animal Trail~
DESCR
As you come to the end of the animal trail, the ancient forest seems to be
thinning, but only because the brush and scrubs don't get enough sunlight to
survive.  The mature forest area is full of thick tree trunks and plain dirt
paths, where the animal trails seem to split and merge.  Because the brush is
clearer you can see plainly where the ancient road continues to lead this
way.As you come upon the edge of this ancient forest, you see a beautiful wildflower filled field to the south and est.  The forest is more of the same to the east, leading back to the animal trails you just came from.~
