EDESC well stone bucket~
The old well is ringed in the same melted-looking mountain stone as the cottage.
Peering over the lip you find no water at all -- only darkness, and far below,
the faint dull glint of coins caught in the mud, small wishes dropped by
travellers who passed this lonely way.~
End

#31038
NAME   Down the Well~
DESCR
You climb down the slick stones of the well shaft into damp, close dark.  But
instead of water, the shaft opens partway down onto a dry side passage -- cut on
purpose, its walls too square to be any accident of nature.  Cold air breathes
out of it, carrying a faint metallic tang.  Whoever sank this well was hiding
far more than water at the bottom of it.
~
