#31042
NAME   End Of The Road~
DESCR
The road abruptly ends here at a broken stone wall that seems to have fallen
into disrepair just like the approaching road.  A few of the walls stones have
come looe from the mortar holding it together, showing the original lumber
beneath used to support it.  To the west there is a small meadow of red sandy
dirt with sparse vegtetation.  The meadow goes a ways to the west, and to the
north.  To the south the forest is tick enough that it doesn't seem reasonable
to pass, and to the north the looming mountains tower over everything, including the clouds.
~
