DESCR
There is no pretending this is a cave any longer.  The walls, floor, and curved
ceiling are all a single seamless surface of dull silver metal, cool and faintly
warm at the same time.  Your footsteps ring softly and come back wrong, somehow
flattened.  The tunnel runs straight and level, lit by no lamp you can find and
yet lit all the same.
~
