#31050
NAME   The Odd Metal Door~
DESCR
The tunnel ends at a single vast disc of silver metal, taller than three men and
set flush into the wall without hinge or handle.  Its face is graven with
concentric rings of symbols that crawl slowly around their circles, and a band of
them near the centre tracks the sun outside as surely as any sundial.  For most
of the day the disc stands shut fast and cold -- but the markings promise it was
built to open, once and briefly, when the sun climbs highest.~
