#31056
NAME   A Small Path Through The Woods~
DESCR
A footpath winds in beneath the eaves of the forest, soft with fallen needles
and dappled with shifting light.  The trees close overhead into a green-gold
roof, and the noise of the open field falls away behind you into a deep woodland
hush.  The path leads on southward, toward a stillness that feels almost
expectant.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   3
DOOR 0
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31054
DOOR 2
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31057
End

#31057
NAME   A Small Path Through The Woods~
DESCR
The forest presses close on both sides here, old and thick-trunked, the
undergrowth heavy with fern and moss.  The path narrows to a single worn line of
bare earth.  Somewhere ahead the ordinary sounds of the wood -- birdsong, the
tick of insects -- thin out and grow strangely hushed, as though the trees
themselves had stopped to listen.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   3
DOOR 0
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31056
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31058
End

#31058
NAME   An Ancient Apple Tree~
DESCR
Beneath the leaves of this ancient apple tree you see hundreds of apples in
various stages of rotting.  It's obvious that no one has tended this tree in
some time.  Nearby you see the stump of a rotten apple tree that seems to have
rotted and fallen over.  Yet something here is wrong.  The air beneath the boughs
hangs strangely thick, and the light seems to lag a beat behind the swaying of
the leaves, as though it were reaching you a heartbeat too late.  Look long
enough and you could swear the fallen, rotted stump and this living tree are
somehow the same tree, caught at two different ends of its life at once.~
FLAGS  0
Sect   3
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31059
DOOR 3
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31057
End

#31059
NAME   The Rotting Apple Tree~
DESCR
This apple tree stump is surrounded by branches of a once great tree, now laid
low.  It's branches would have been at least a hundred feet high.  Now the
branches are strewn about this glade, some so rotten that they've been overcome
with moss and fungus.  You see something odd and faded etched into the base of
the trunk.  The air around the fallen trunk shivers faintly, like heat over
summer stone, though the glade is cold.  For just a moment, at the edge of your
vision, the rotted wood seems whole and green again -- and then it is gone, and
only the ruin remains.  Whatever happened here, time itself has not entirely
healed over it.~
FLAGS  0
Sect   3
DOOR 3
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31058
EDESC odd etching~
Though it's very faded, you can make out the shape of a heart with the initials M and E carved in the middle.  The E seems to have been worn smooth.
~
End

#31060
NAME   In The Pond~
DESCR
The pond is still and clear, small minnows and insects swimming through being
busy with their errands.  The silt at the bottom of the pond is drab and brown,
undisturbed aside from your presence.  Above you can see the surface of the pond
just above you.  There are various sticks and branches in the mud, and you notice something glinting in the silt.~
FLAGS  0
Sect   0
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31061
DOOR 4
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31026
EDESC silt mud glinting box~
This silver box is half buried in the silt, but you can make out the letter E embellished on the lid.  Upon closer inspection you can make out the inscription "Elia", though when you open it the box is in fact empty.~
End

#31061
NAME   Under The Dock~
DESCR
As you squeeze underneath the dock you find yourself cramped and unable to move
well.  The mud here is thick and visibility is low.  Above you can see the
boards of the dock rippling above the smooth surface of the pond as light peeks
its way through the boards, but you cannot see much else in the murky water.~
FLAGS  2049
Sect   6
DOOR 3
You can see the end of the dock past the debris and mud.~
~
0 0 31060
End

#31062
NAME   The Crumbling Road~
DESCR
The road is little more than a suggestion now, a scatter of cracked stones losing
their long fight with the forest floor.  Ahead to the west the trees begin to
thin, and you can sense open ground beyond -- the true end of the road, where
whatever this way once led has crumbled away into ruin.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   11
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31063
DOOR 3
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31042
End

#31063
NAME   The Overgrown Road~
DESCR
The old road runs on beneath a heavy canopy, a green tunnel dim even at midday.
Roots have buckled the paving into low waves, and pale mushrooms grow in the damp
seams between the stones.  The air is cool and still, and smells of leaf-mould
and slow, patient decay.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   11
DOOR 0
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31064
DOOR 3
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31062
End

#31064
NAME   The Overgrown Road~
DESCR
Here the forest has all but reclaimed the road.  Saplings stand in the middle of
what was once the way, and only the odd cobblestone breaking the leaf litter
proves a road ran through at all.  You push through low branches, following the
faint straight line the trees have never quite managed to erase.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   11
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31065
DOOR 2
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31063
End

#31065
NAME   A Bend In The Old Road~
DESCR
The road bends sharply here around a shoulder of rock, the reason for the turn
long since forgotten.  Moss furs the stones a deep, soft green and muffles your
steps.  It is very quiet -- no birds, no wind to speak of, only the occasional
distant crack of a branch settling somewhere back among the trees.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   11
DOOR 2
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31066
DOOR 3
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31064
End

#31066
NAME   The Rough Road~
DESCR
The old road climbs a low rise here, its stones heaved and tilted by frost and
root.  Brambles reach in from either side to snag at your legs.  A fallen road
marker lies half-swallowed in the grass, its carved lettering worn far too
smooth to read.  The mountains loom grey and patient beyond the trees.
~
