Sect   11
DOOR 0
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31065
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31067
End

#31067
NAME   The Rough Road~
DESCR
The last of the maintained cobblestone gives out here, and the road turns rough
and broken underfoot.  Weeds push up thick between the surviving stones, and deep
ruts run where the rains have carried the surface away.  Behind you to the east
the road still remembers being cared for; ahead to the west, it plainly does not.
~
FLAGS  0
Sect   11
DOOR 1
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31043
DOOR 3
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31066
End

#31068
NAME   The Threshold~
DESCR
As you enter from the waiting room, the entrance seals shut.  The smooth surface
of this almost tubular room has windows that seem to flicker with strange
energeies outside intermittently.  The room is bare of anything other than a
ledge large enough to sit on on each side of the room.  The lighting in this
room seems to come from under the ledge, although when you look there is no
noticeable source for the under-lighting.  There is a sundial in the center of
the tube on a small pedestal made of the same metal as all the rest of the
chamber, however the sundial seems to cast a shadow as if it were standing
directly in the sun.  

12-2: Stellar/Astral

12-2: Hourglass

2-4: Pendulum

4-6: Heat

6-8: Lightning

8-10: Looping

10-12: Predictive~
FLAGS  0
Sect   0
DOOR 0
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31070
DOOR 2
You see nothing special here.~
~
0 0 31051
EDESC sundial shadow~
NOTE: This should change depending on what time it is to indicate which area you'll get into after this.

This small silvery sundial is incredibly minimalistic in it's design.  At the moment the small triangular spike seems to be casting a shadow at the %s oclock mark.

12-2: Stellar/Astral
12-2: Hourglass
2-4: Pendulum
4-6: Heat
6-8: Lightning
8-10: Looping
10-12: Predictive

Each of these areas will have a puzzle you ahve to solve to get out, and a hidden piece of his "final work" that will remove him from time entirely, but he can't do it himself without creating a paradox, so this entire area that started as a trap actually became his way of removing himself from time to prevent a paradox that he eventually sees coming in the predictive time area.

It should progressively get tougher and tougher as you go forward in time closer to the paradox.~
EDESC stellar astral~
12-2: Stellar/Astral - This period of the lab will outline his obsession with the stars and astral relationships that dictate the passing of time.  You'll find notes about his ramblings of relativistic nature of time, how movement plays into it, and puzzles related to stars, sun, and moon positions.  Would be cool to add something in here with a legitimate lunar calendar.

In this area you'll actually find the silver box from under the pond with his wife's name - this is some foreshadowing, but each piece of time you'll have to use something on this box to actually build out the final "piece" that will prevent the paradox and get you a reward - so if you don't keep it with you you won't have pieces to apply to it, etc.~
EDESC hourglass~
The hourglass lab is when he's past the relativistic research and is starting to look at practical application of time passing.  You'll find puzzles and notes related to practical application of moving forward or backwards of objects in time, but not yet himself.  He's studied enough to demonstrate that time travel of objects is possible, but not brave enough or crazy enough to have tried it on himself.  You'll find the first notes from his friend in this one, but wont meet him yet.  ~
EDESC pendulum~
The pendulum era of the lab is going to be more mad-scientist and you'll meet the friend in this timeframe.  He's still alive and well, but focused on trying to decipher his friends research to "catch up" to him through the time jumps.  This area of the lab is going to be more like gnomish artificer where he's discovering ways to intentionally impact the flow of time, not just move himself, but to actually alter the flow of time around him and impact it in different ways.  Puzzles in this section will be related to building a basic clock with a pendulum - finding all the pieces and put it together - the pieces are in various spots in the lab.  You'll also start to find automatons in this area that are like gnomish artificer automatons and notes showing that he needed to build helpers to assist in building things, etc.  These will be mobs you can fight, some will have the pieces of the clock that solve the riddle, etc.  ~
EDESC heat~
The "heat" area is when he starts to get into energy manipulation for measuring and manipulating time directly, but harnessing natural elements to power the various aspects of his time research.  This area is the first area where he will start to notice that his experiments and alterations on time are having stability impacts in other areas of time, and while here you will be able to "observe" destabilization affects.  This is the area where he is trying to increase the power for his experiments, because now that he knows how to control minute aspects of time, he needs more and more power to fuel the experiments.~
EDESC lightning~
The "lightning" area will be sort of a hint at a digital concept of time - at this point he's harnessed power and has focused on precision - so the electrical aspect of time is going to be solving puzzles like binary gate addition/subtraction to unlock the way back with your prize. ~
EDESC Looping~
In the loopin time he's beginning to experiment with paradoxes and how to create and avoid them.  This part of the lab will actually be where the friend is killed, but never actually dies, because the lab itself is in a looped paradox - the actual trap.  This is where you'll see some of the insanity and risk - something happened prior to this that made him start to take insane risks, something we later will find out that his dear Elia dies, and he's trying to find a way to save her.~
EDESC predictive~
New extra description.
~
End

